---
/**
 * Simulators. Ported to the converged Paper design 2026-08-03 (FW-3967); spec in
 * `design/SUBPAGE-EXPLORATION.md`.
 *
 * **The idea: the machine measures things, so the page does too.** A bay
 * schematic, the readings named on the part of the machine that takes them, and
 * a handedness row that draws the unknown at the same size as the known.
 *
 * **Name the readings; do not count them.** This is a correction, not a style
 * choice. Three different counts for one machine shipped across this project:
 * this page said five, the Paper design committed to four diagrams, and
 * GolfZon's own sensors page lists more than either depending on how you group
 * them. No source says four. A reading with a NAME on it is a better diagram
 * than a total, and it cannot be contradicted by a recount — so nothing on this
 * page states how many there are (truth-audit.md §C6).
 *
 * Name the technology: 42% of the segment names none, and GolfZon is a search
 * term with real credibility weight (playbook-core.md §8, playbook-sim-venue.md
 * §4). The client's position, 2026-08-04: golfers want to know what the
 * technology IS, not have it hidden behind a house brand — which is what the
 * nearest comparable venue does (see FW-3992).
 *
 * ⚠️ TrackMan and Full Swing may be named ONLY inside content arguing why
 * GolfZon is better, framed as our opinion. They used to appear here as a
 * neutral "what else you'll see around the Twin Cities" aside; that framing is
 * retired (client-answers.md §7).
 *
 * ⚠️ RESOLVED 2026-08-04 — this was the single most consequential unconfirmed
 * fact on the site, and it is now settled: **GolfZon TwoVision NX, tour spec**
 * (client-answers.md §7).
 *
 * The history, kept because it explains the redirects and the AEO cleanup: the
 * client's current pages said "GolfZon", while /home-old, /home-2 and
 * /news/golfzon-twovision — all still live, all still indexed — said "6 GolfZon
 * TwoVision simulators", and AI search summaries were repeating TwoVision back
 * at people (seo-map.md §0). Turned out the older pages were closer: it is a
 * TwoVision NX. Everything downstream — schema, titles, the homepage hero —
 * inherits this, so change it here first.
 *
 * ⚠️ Stillwater's blanks are all *Pending confirmation*, never *Not yet set*.
 * Settled by the human (FW-3967 §"Three decisions"): Stillwater is an operating
 * venue that knows how its own room is laid out. Nothing there is undecided; it
 * is unverified, and those are different promises to a reader.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookButton from '../components/venue/BookButton.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/venue/SectionHead.astro';
import HeroStrip from '../components/venue/HeroStrip.astro';
import ReadoutCell from '../components/venue/ReadoutCell.astro';
import GapCell from '../components/venue/GapCell.astro';
import PendingTag from '../components/venue/PendingTag.astro';
import StubNote from '../components/venue/StubNote.astro';
import BaySchematic from '../components/venue/BaySchematic.astro';
import HandednessRow from '../components/venue/HandednessRow.astro';
import { buttonClasses } from '../lib/buttons';
import { getVenues, venuePath } from '../lib/venues';

const venues = await getVenues();
const lakeville = venues.find((v) => v.data.slug === 'lakeville');
const stillwater = venues.find((v) => v.data.slug === 'stillwater');
const totalBays = venues.reduce((n, v) => n + v.data.bays, 0);

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'GolfZon Simulator Bays — Lakeville & Stillwater MN',
  metaDescription:
    'Ten GolfZon bays in Lakeville and Stillwater MN — a tilting swing plate, auto tee-up and real ball flight. Five of the six Lakeville bays suit lefties.',
};

/**
 * The readings, by the part of the machine that takes them. GolfZon's own, from
 * golfzongolf.com/global/user/technology/sensors.do.
 *
 * ⚠️ "Club face impact area" is what GolfZon publishes. Do NOT put "face angle"
 * back — it is not a metric they claim, and it was removed once already
 * (truth-audit §U19). And do not add a count anywhere near these lists.
 */
const CLUB_READINGS = ['Club path', 'Angle of attack', 'Club face impact area'];
const BALL_READINGS = ['Ball speed', 'Direction and trajectory', 'Spin rate', 'Launch angle', 'Spin axis'];

/**
 * What the hardware does, for someone who has never used one. Titles are the
 * client's own homepage feature bullets; the bodies are constrained to what
 * GolfZon publishes about its own sensors, because this is the one section whose
 * job is to sound like it knows the machine. The plate detail ("five-segment",
 * fairway/rough/bunker mats) is likewise GolfZon's own and replaced an invented
 * "in a bunker shot it drops".
 *
 * NOTE the ordering claim in the sensor bullet: the cameras are "positioned
 * above and in FRONT of the player" and "meet at 90 degrees" — not "above and
 * beside you", which is what this said before.
 */
const hardware = [
  [
    'A moving swing plate',
    'The floor you stand on tilts to match the lie. GolfZon builds it in five segments — one under the ball, four under your stance — with fairway, rough and bunker mats. That is the part people do not expect, and it is why the ball behaves like it does outdoors rather than like a video game.',
  ],
  [
    'Auto tee-up and ball return',
    'The machine tees the next ball for you. You do not bend down between shots, and you do not run out of balls — they are included, and you never bring your own.',
  ],
  [
    'A touchscreen next to you',
    'You pick the course and the settings from the screen in the bay, and it scores the round for you. Staff set it up on your first visit; you do not need to know anything going in.',
  ],
  [
    'Nothing attached to you',
    'No tags on the club, nothing clipped to your belt, no calibration ritual. You walk in, and the bay is already watching the ball.',
  ],
];

/** Practice and play are different products in the same bay. No numerals — not steps. */
const modes = [
  [
    'Play a course',
    'Eighteen holes on a real course, rendered hole by hole. Budget about an hour per person — four of you in one bay is roughly a four-hour round, which is why most groups play nine or split across two bays.',
  ],
  [
    'Practise',
    'A driving range and a putting green with no queue, no weather and no lost balls. Every shot comes back with numbers, which is the point — you find out what your 7-iron actually carries instead of what you tell people it carries.',
  ],
  [
    'Play a game',
    'Closest-to-the-pin, longest drive, and the arcade-style formats. This is what a group who do not really golf ends up playing, and it is fine.',
  ],
];

/**
 * Stillwater's unverified specifics. Each one is something the venue knows and
 * we have not confirmed — the middle mark, every time.
 */
const stillwaterPending = [
  ['Left-handed bays', 'How many of the four bays are set up for left-handers. Lakeville has five of six.'],
  ['Screens', 'The TV count in the room. Lakeville has nine.'],
  ['Seating', 'How many people the room seats, and whether the bowling side can take the overflow.'],
  ['Club rental', 'Whether rental sets are available there at all, and whether they are the $15 Lakeville charges.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  {/* 1. HERO + the 4-cell strip. */}
  <section class="on-dark bg-midnight">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter pt-s8 pb-s7 lg:px-gutter-lg lg:pt-s9 lg:pb-s8">
      <p class="caps-label text-amber">GolfZon · Lakeville &amp; Stillwater</p>
      <h1 class="mt-s5 text-hero leading-hero font-extrabold tracking-display-tight text-white">The bays</h1>
      <p class="mt-s5 max-w-prose-page border-l-slab border-amber pl-s4 text-lead leading-body text-paper">
        You hit a real ball with a real club into a screen. The floor under you tilts to match the lie, a sensor in that
        floor reads the ball, and cameras overhead read the club. Nothing is strapped to you and nothing needs setting
        up.
      </p>

      <HeroStrip
        class="mt-s8"
        tone="dark"
        cells={[
          { label: 'Bays', value: String(totalBays), qualifier: 'across two venues' },
          { label: 'Lefty-friendly', value: '5 of 6', qualifier: 'at Lakeville — one bay is right-handed only' },
          { label: 'Balls', value: 'Included', qualifier: 'every bay has its own — never bring your own' },
          {
            label: 'Course list',
            gap: {
              state: 'notSet',
              reason:
                'A "240+ courses" figure exists only on two retired homepages and is not repeated on the current site, so we do not republish it.',
            },
          },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* 2. THE MACHINE. The schematic and the named readings — the page's central
      idea, and the section that has to be physically correct. See BaySchematic
      for why the ball arrows point UP. */
  }
  <section class="on-dark bg-midnight">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead tone="dark" index={1}>What the machine reads</SectionHead>
      <p class="max-w-prose-page text-lead leading-body text-paper">
        Every bay runs a GolfZon TwoVision NX — the current model. Two different parts of it are watching, and they are
        watching two different things.
      </p>

      <BaySchematic class="mt-s7" club={CLUB_READINGS} ball={BALL_READINGS} />

      <p class="mt-s6 max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-paper">
        That is why the numbers mean something. The ball data is measured off the ball itself rather than inferred from
        the swing, so what comes back is what actually happened.
      </p>

      {
        /* Tour spec is a real claim and it needs both halves. GolfZon's tour
          requires a TwoVision or TwoVisionNX AND a Dual Plate or Motion Plate;
          confirmed 2026-08-04 that we have both, so the line can be written.
          Until then the intake note said we would not write it, and we did not. */
      }
      <div class="mt-s7 flex flex-wrap gap-s7 border-t-hairline border-slate pt-s5">
        <ReadoutCell label="System" tone="dark" size="name">GolfZon TwoVision NX</ReadoutCell>
        <ReadoutCell label="Specification" tone="dark" size="name">Tour spec</ReadoutCell>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-s5 max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-paper">
        The same equipment GolfZon requires for its own tour — the current TwoVision NX with the motion plate under you.
        Not an older unit with a new badge on it.
      </p>

      <StubNote
        class="mt-s7"
        needs="Still needed from GolfZon: the current course count, and five or six named courses people would recognise. A comparable venue publishes '100+', which makes the retired '240+' on the client's old pages look stale rather than merely unsourced."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 3. WHAT IS WHERE, per venue — including who can play in which bay. */}
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={2}>What is where</SectionHead>
      <p class="max-w-prose-page text-lead leading-body text-inkBody">
        Ten bays across two rooms. Lakeville has been open since 2022 and is written up here down to which bay a lefty
        gets. Stillwater opened in 2026, and the marks below are the details still being confirmed for this page rather
        than things the room has not decided.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-s6 grid gap-s8 border-t-score border-navy pt-s6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        {/* LAKEVILLE — known, in detail. */}
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink">
            <a
              href={lakeville ? venuePath(lakeville) : '/locations/lakeville/'}
              class="underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 transition-colors duration-fast ease-standard hover:text-ember"
            >
              {lakeville?.data.name}
            </a>
          </h3>

          <div class="mt-s5 flex flex-wrap gap-s7">
            <ReadoutCell label="Bays" size="xl">{lakeville?.data.bays}</ReadoutCell>
            <ReadoutCell label="Screens" size="xl">9</ReadoutCell>
            <ReadoutCell label="Seats" size="xl">36</ReadoutCell>
          </div>

          <p class="caps-label mt-s6 text-label-sm text-inkMuted">Which bays a lefty can play</p>
          <HandednessRow class="mt-s3" bays={['both', 'both', 'both', 'both', 'both', 'right']} />
          <p class="mt-s4 max-w-prose-page text-small leading-body text-inkBody">
            Five of the six take either handedness; the sixth is right-handed only. If you are a lefty in a group of
            six, say so when you book and we will put you in the right bay.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-s6">
            <ReadoutCell label="Club rental" size="name">$15 a set</ReadoutCell>
            <p class="mt-s2 max-w-prose-page text-small leading-body text-inkMuted">
              Basic sets, not fitted. Bring your own clubs if you have them.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-s6"><BookButton venue={lakeville} size="sm" variant="outline" /></div>
        </div>

        {/* STILLWATER — the same diagram, with the parts we cannot vouch for marked. */}
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink">
            <a
              href={stillwater ? venuePath(stillwater) : '/locations/stillwater/'}
              class="underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 transition-colors duration-fast ease-standard hover:text-ember"
            >
              {stillwater?.data.name}
            </a>
          </h3>

          <div class="mt-s5 flex flex-wrap gap-s7">
            <ReadoutCell label="Bays" size="xl">{stillwater?.data.bays}</ReadoutCell>
          </div>

          <p class="caps-label mt-s6 text-label-sm text-inkMuted">Which bays a lefty can play</p>
          <HandednessRow
            class="mt-s3"
            bays={['unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown']}
            pendingReason="We have not confirmed how many of Stillwater's four bays take left-handers. The venue knows; we have asked. Until it comes back we would rather draw four question marks than guess on your behalf."
          />

          <ul class="mt-s6 border-t-hairline border-navy">
            {
              stillwaterPending.map(([what, why]) => (
                <li class="border-b-hairline border-navy py-s4">
                  <p class="caps-label text-label-sm text-inkMuted">{what}</p>
                  <PendingTag class="mt-s2" reason={why} />
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>

          <div class="mt-s6"><BookButton venue={stillwater} size="sm" variant="outline" /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 4. THE HARDWARE, explained. Rows at one scale — a set of things, so no numerals. */}
  <section class="bg-greige">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={3}>What separates it from hitting into a net</SectionHead>
      <dl class="border-t-score border-navy">
        {
          hardware.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div class="grid gap-s3 border-b-hairline border-navy py-row md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] md:gap-s6">
              <dt class="font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-inkBody">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 5. WHAT YOU CAN DO WITH IT. */}
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={4}>Practice, play, or just mess about</SectionHead>
      <dl class="border-t-score border-navy">
        {
          modes.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div class="grid gap-s3 border-b-hairline border-navy py-row md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] md:gap-s6">
              <dt class="font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-inkBody">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <div class="mt-s7 max-w-prose-page">
        <GapCell
          label="Courses on the machines"
          state="notSet"
          size="name"
          reason='A "240+ courses and 6 arcade games" figure exists only on two retired homepages and is not repeated on the current site, so we do not republish it. We have asked for the current list.'
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 6. NEVER USED ONE. The largest addressable market (playbook-core.md §8). */}
  <section class="on-dark bg-midnight">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead tone="dark" index={5}>Never used one?</SectionHead>
      <p class="max-w-prose-page text-lead leading-body text-paper">
        Staff start the bay for you and show you the screen. Turn the difficulty down, turn the wind off, and take as
        many shots as you like — there is no group behind you and the bay is yours for the hour. If you top one, the
        machine tees another ball up.
      </p>
      <p
        class="mt-s6 max-w-prose-page border-y-score border-amber py-s4 font-display text-row leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-white"
      >
        You do not need clubs, you do not need shoes, and you do not need to know the rules.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-s7">
        <p class="text-body leading-body text-paper">
          A bay is $35 an hour through 30 September 2026 — per bay, not per person, up to six of you.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-s5 flex flex-wrap gap-s4">
          <BookButton size="lg" variant="onDark" />
          <a href="/rates/" class={buttonClasses('lg', 'ghostDark')}>See rates &amp; hours</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
